<title>USA: United Illuminating Q4 shr falls w/charge.</title>
<headline>United Illuminating Q4 shr falls w/charge.</headline>
<dateline>NEW HAVEN, Conn. 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr net		$    0.04		   $ 0.46</p>
<p> Shr operating	     0.22		     0.24</p>
<p> Net			    588		    6,614</p>
<p> Revs		     177,203		  161,314</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,101		   14,099</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr net		  $  2.88		   $ 3.64</p>
<p> Shr operating	     3.94		     3.61</p>
<p> Net			 39,096		   50,393</p>
<p> Revs		     726,020		  690,449</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,101		   14,090</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: The United Illuminating Co reported a charge of $2.6 million after tax, or $0.18 a share, in 1996's fourth quarter to make provision for losses associated with agent collections and other items at its American Payment Systems Inc unit.</p>
<p>The company also recorded a charge for 1996 of $1.09 a share, including $0.95 a share for early retirements and voluntary separations arising from restructuring and cost-cutting efforts.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk, (212) 859-1610))</p>
